        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/28051/comment/54793",
          "id": "54793",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=tripod",
            "name": "tripod",
            "key": "tripod",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636"
            },
            "displayName": "Tobias Bocanegra",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Tokyo"
          },
          "body": "The concept here is, that the PersistentNodeState should not be to intelligent, it is rather managed from outside. so store() will store and does not repsect the status.\nthe performance bottleneck in versioning is caused by the PersistenNode, which is a helper class for easily modifying persistent node states and in the PersistentVersionManager. the status of the underlaying node state should be respected there.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=tripod",
            "name": "tripod",
            "key": "tripod",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636"
            },
            "displayName": "Tobias Bocanegra",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Tokyo"
          },
          "created": "2004-10-29T08:18:00.000+0000",
          "updated": "2004-10-29T08:18:00.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/28051/comment/54799",
          "id": "54799",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=fmeschbe",
            "name": "fmeschbe",
            "key": "fmeschbe",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Felix Meschberger",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "> so store() will store and does not repsect the status.\n\nOk, but why does it use the status to decide on which event to send ?? As it may be the case that the instance is not modified, an updated message does not make sense to me. On the other hand, there is not enough JavaDoc for me to know it :-)",
